hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-10 : List (List Word)
hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-10 = cons "*Code* is from Latin *codex*, a tree trunk, then a block of wooden tablets, then a book, then a body of law, and only last a cipher and a program. Code was law before it was software, and a book before it was law. A *program* is Greek *pro* + *graphein*, written before: a public notice posted in advance. So code is a book of law written in advance. The safety claim in hyperactivity is that the law can be checked against the book before anything runs." (cons "" nil)
